{"schemaVersion":1,"key":"intermediate/ui","track":"everyone","lang":"en","dir":"ltr","title":"Agentic UI","words":1869,"objectives":{"lang":"en","items":["Say what agentic UI is, and how it differs from a normal app and a chat box","Explain why an agent's work is shown step by step instead of all at the end","Explain what AG-UI is for, using the universal plug from Code Agents as the picture","Say what human in the loop means, and why an agent stops to ask you before a step that matters"]},"translatedObjectives":null,"prerequisites":[{"key":"intermediate/loop-engineering","number":14,"title":"Loop Engineering","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"}],"previous":{"key":"intermediate/loop-engineering","number":14,"title":"Loop Engineering","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"next":{"key":"intermediate/security","number":16,"title":"Security","drawn":true,"track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"toc":[{"id":"why-this-matters-to-you","text":"Why This Matters to You","depth":2},{"id":"what-agentic-ui-is","text":"What Agentic UI is","depth":2},{"id":"why-stream-the-run","text":"Why Stream the Run","depth":2},{"id":"what-gets-streamed","text":"What Gets Streamed","depth":2},{"id":"every-agent-speaks-its-own-format","text":"Every Agent Speaks Its Own Format","depth":2},{"id":"ag-ui","text":"AG-UI","depth":2},{"id":"who-supports-it","text":"Who Supports It","depth":3},{"id":"the-agent-protocol-stack","text":"The Agent Protocol Stack","depth":2},{"id":"human-in-the-loop","text":"Human in the Loop","depth":2},{"id":"beyond-streaming","text":"Beyond Streaming","depth":2},{"id":"words-you-now-know","text":"Words You Now Know","depth":2},{"id":"summary","text":"Summary","depth":2},{"id":"references","text":"References","depth":2},{"id":"-articles","text":"📄 Articles","depth":3},{"id":"️-tools","text":"🛠️ Tools","depth":3}],"body":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"intermediate/loop-engineering","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Loop Engineering"}]},{"type":"text","text":" ended with agents that work for minutes, hours, and sometimes days. Someone still has to look at that work: see what the agent is doing, stop it when it goes wrong, and approve the steps that matter. This module is about the screen where that happens."}],"lead":true},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-this-matters-to-you","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Why This Matters to You"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Many AI assistants at work show their progress on a screen: \"searching\", \"reading the file\", \"writing the report\". When that screen is built well, you can follow the agent, catch a mistake early, and step in. This module explains how that screen gets the agent's work, and why many of the companies building these products now use one shared way to do it."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-agentic-ui-is","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"What Agentic UI is"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"CopilotKit, a company that builds these interfaces, defines it like this:"}]},{"type":"quote","blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Agentic UI is user interface built for humans and AI agents to work in the same application."}]},{"type":"text","text":" It streams agent work as it happens, accepts human steering and approvals mid-run, renders agent-generated interface alongside developer-built components, and keeps application state synchronized between the user and the agent."}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"In plain words, the difference is who is doing the work:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A normal app"}]},{"type":"text","text":" waits for you. You press a button, and the same thing happens every time."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A chat box"}]},{"type":"text","text":" answers once. You type a question, you wait, and one reply appears."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"An agentic UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":" shows an agent that is already working. It makes many decisions and uses many tools, and you watch it, guide it, and correct it while it works."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"This module covers the base of all of this: "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"showing the agent's work as it happens"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and the agent "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"stopping to ask you"}]},{"type":"text","text":" before a step that matters. The parts where you steer the agent while it works, or where the agent designs the screen itself, come in the Expert level."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"why-stream-the-run","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Why Stream the Run"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Think of ordering food with a delivery app. You can wait at the door with no idea what is happening. Or the app shows you each step: order received, being prepared, on the way, at your door. The food arrives at the same time either way. But in the second case you know what is going on, and if something goes wrong, you find out early."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"An agent works the same way. A model writes its answer one word at a time, as "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/llms","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"LLM Fundamentals"}]},{"type":"text","text":" showed. An agent also thinks, uses a tool, waits for the result, and uses another tool. The whole job can take a minute or an hour. So there are two ways to build the screen:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Wait, then show everything."}]},{"type":"text","text":" You look at a spinning wheel the whole time and cannot tell whether the agent is working, stuck, or going the wrong way."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Stream the run."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The screen shows each piece of work as soon as it exists: a few words of the answer, \"now checking the weather\", the result. This is called "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"streaming"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent products such as chat assistants and coding agents stream. The work happens step by step anyway, so there is no reason to hide it. And seeing the steps lets you stop a job that is going wrong while it is still cheap."}]},{"type":"image","number":"15.1","title":"A streaming agent interface","note":"The screen starts with an empty prompt. Once the agent starts, a checklist of its steps fills in, and each step is ticked off as the agent finishes it, so you see progress instead of a spinner.","src":"course-images/intermediate/streaming-ui.webp","alt":"A streaming agent interface","width":1280,"height":720},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-gets-streamed","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"What Gets Streamed"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The agent's side (the "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"backend"}]},{"type":"text","text":") does not send one long piece of text. It sends many small messages called "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"events"}]},{"type":"text","text":", each saying what just happened. The screen (the "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"frontend"}]},{"type":"text","text":") reads each event and updates itself. For the weather question from "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/tools","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Tool Calling"}]},{"type":"text","text":":"}]},{"type":"diagram","number":"15.2","title":"What Gets Streamed","svg":{"light":"api/v1/diagrams/b4ecf6fa8a66eaad0a914f31e832dddb.svg","dark":"api/v1/diagrams/757f7515e944efe88a2cde26ddb8f841.svg"}},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The kinds of event are the same in almost every agent:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"the job started or finished"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"a piece of the answer"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"the agent's thinking"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"a tool being used, and its result"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"a helper agent (a "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"subagent"}]},{"type":"text","text":") starting or finishing"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"the current state of the work"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"every-agent-speaks-its-own-format","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Every Agent Speaks Its Own Format"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Here is the problem. The kinds of event are similar everywhere, but each agent product writes them in its own format, with its own names. So the screen has to be built for one specific agent. If the company later switches to a different agent, the screen has to be rebuilt too, even if it should look exactly the same."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Engineers try hard to avoid this kind of tie between two parts. Remember the universal charger plug from "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"intermediate/coding-agents","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Code Agents"}]},{"type":"text","text":": MCP lets one tool work with every agent. The same idea, used between the agent and the screen, is AG-UI."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"ag-ui","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":" stands for the "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Agent–User Interaction Protocol"}]},{"type":"text","text":". A "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"protocol"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is an agreed set of rules for how two systems talk. AG-UI is an open, shared list of events. An agent that speaks AG-UI can send them, and a screen built for AG-UI can show them. So the company can change the agent behind the screen at any time."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Some of its events, by name:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"code","text":"RunStarted"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"code","text":"RunFinished"},{"type":"text","text":": the job starts and ends."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"code","text":"TextMessageContent"},{"type":"text","text":": a piece of the answer."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"code","text":"ToolCallStart"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"code","text":"ToolCallResult"},{"type":"text","text":": a tool is used, and what it returned."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"code","text":"SubagentStarted"},{"type":"text","text":": a helper agent begins."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"If you are curious, this is what the weather job looks like as AG-UI events, one line per event. On the wire each name is written in capitals, so "},{"type":"code","text":"RunStarted"},{"type":"text","text":" becomes "},{"type":"code","text":"RUN_STARTED"},{"type":"text","text":". It is fine to skip it:"}]},{"type":"code","language":"json","lines":[[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"RUN_STARTED\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"threadId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"t1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"runId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"r1\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TEXT_MESSAGE_START\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"role\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"assistant\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"delta\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"Let me check the weather...\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TEXT_MESSAGE_END\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m1\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TOOL_CALL_START\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"toolCallId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"c1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"toolCallName\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"get_weather\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TOOL_CALL_ARGS\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"toolCallId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"c1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"delta\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"{","role":"string"},{"text":"\\\"","role":"number"},{"text":"city","role":"string"},{"text":"\\\"","role":"number"},{"text":": ","role":"string"},{"text":"\\\"","role":"number"},{"text":"Istanbul","role":"string"},{"text":"\\\"","role":"number"},{"text":"}\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TOOL_CALL_END\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"toolCallId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"c1\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TOOL_CALL_RESULT\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m2\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"toolCallId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"c1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"content\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"34°C\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TEXT_MESSAGE_START\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m3\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"role\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"assistant\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TEXT_MESSAGE_CONTENT\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m3\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"delta\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"It is 34°C in Istanbul.\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"TEXT_MESSAGE_END\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"messageId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"m3\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}],[{"text":"{"},{"text":"\"type\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"RUN_FINISHED\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"threadId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"t1\"","role":"string"},{"text":", "},{"text":"\"runId\"","role":"string"},{"text":": "},{"text":"\"r1\"","role":"string"},{"text":"}"}]]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"who-supports-it","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Who Supports It"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Because the list is shared, many agent products speak it. LangChain and CrewAI are partners. Microsoft's and Google's agent kits support it directly. The Claude Agent SDK and the OpenAI Agents SDK support it through community projects. The CopilotKit team develops it together with its partners."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"the-agent-protocol-stack","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The Agent Protocol Stack"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI is one of three shared protocols, and each one connects the agent to a different side."}]},{"type":"image","number":"15.3","title":"The agent protocol stack: MCP, A2A and AG-UI","note":"The agent sits in the middle. MCP and A2A reach left, to its tools and to other agents. AG-UI reaches right, to the people using the app.","src":"course-images/intermediate/ag-ui-mcp.webp","alt":"The agent protocol stack: MCP, A2A and AG-UI","width":1600,"height":923},{"type":"table","number":"15.1","title":"The Agent Protocol Stack","rowHeaders":false,"align":[null,null],"head":[{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Protocol"}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Connects the agent to"}]}],"rows":[[{"inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"MCP"}]}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"tools and data"}]}],[{"inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A2A"}]}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"other agents"}]}],[{"inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI"}]}]},{"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"the people using the app"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"They work together. A real product often uses all three at once. Do not mix them up: you met MCP in "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"intermediate/coding-agents","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Code Agents"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and A2A in "},{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"module","key":"fundamentals/multi-agent","track":"everyone","lang":"en"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Multi-Agent Systems"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and AG-UI is the third, the one that faces the people."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"human-in-the-loop","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Human in the Loop"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Watching an agent is useful. Being able to say \"yes\" or \"no\" before it acts is even more useful. This is called "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"human in the loop"}]},{"type":"text","text":": you stay in the loop of the work."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Think of a new assistant who writes an email for you. A good assistant does not send it at once. They show it to you, and you approve it, change it, or say no. Then they continue. An agent can work in the same way. It does the routine steps by itself. At a step that matters, such as sending an email, changing a record or paying for something, it stops and waits for you."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"This matters most when a step has real consequences. If you see the step before it runs, you can stop it or fix it. A mistake caught early costs less. That is also why the screen shows the steps."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"On the screen, it works like this. The agent stops. The screen shows what the agent wants to do, with buttons to approve it, to reject it, or to pick one option. Your answer goes back to the agent, and the agent continues from there. AG-UI has a standard way to do this, so any screen can at least show the message text."}]},{"type":"image","number":"15.4","title":"An AI that stops for your answer","note":"The AI offers times for a meeting and stops. It books only after you pick one. In the second try, the person picks \"None of these work\", and the AI says that it could not book.","src":"course-images/intermediate/human-in-the-loop.webp","alt":"An AI that stops for your answer","width":1200,"height":926},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"beyond-streaming","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Beyond Streaming"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Streaming and human in the loop are the base. The Expert level will cover more:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"You can steer the agent while it works."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The screen and the agent can share the same information."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"The agent can design parts of the screen itself ("},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"generative UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":")."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"words-you-now-know","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Words You Now Know"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Agentic UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":": a screen where a person and a working agent use the same app together."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Streaming"}]},{"type":"text","text":": showing the agent's work piece by piece, as it happens."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Event"}]},{"type":"text","text":": one small message saying what just happened, such as \"tool call started\"."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Backend"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"frontend"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the agent's side, and the screen's side."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Protocol"}]},{"type":"text","text":": an agreed set of rules for how two systems talk."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the shared protocol between an agent and the screen."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"MCP"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"A2A"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the shared protocols between an agent and its tools, and between agents."}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Human in the loop"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the agent stops at a step that matters and waits for a person to approve, change or choose."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"summary","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Summary"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Agentic UI is the screen where you and a working agent share an app. Its base is streaming: the agent works step by step, so the screen shows it step by step, like a delivery app showing each stage of your order. Each agent product used its own format, which tied the screen to one agent. AG-UI is a shared format, like a universal plug, so any screen can work with any agent. Next to MCP (tools) and A2A (other agents), it connects the agent to the people using it. And when a step matters, the agent stops and asks you first: that is human in the loop."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"strong","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Quick check"}]},{"type":"text","text":": Why does an agentic UI show the agent's work step by step? What problem does AG-UI solve? And why does an agent sometimes stop and wait for you?"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"references","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"References"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"-articles","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"📄 Articles"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://www.copilotkit.ai/learning/what-is-agentic-ui"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"What Is Agentic UI?"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the definition this module uses"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/introduction"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"AG-UI Overview"}]},{"type":"text","text":": what the protocol is, and who supports it"}]}]},{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://docs.ag-ui.com/concepts/interrupts"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"Interrupts"}]},{"type":"text","text":": how AG-UI stops an agent for a person's answer"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"️-tools","inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"🛠️ Tools"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"blocks":[{"type":"paragraph","inlines":[{"type":"link","target":{"kind":"external","url":"https://dojo.ag-ui.com/"},"inlines":[{"type":"text","text":"CopilotKit Interactive Dojo"}]},{"type":"text","text":": live demos of agentic UI to try in the browser"}]}]}]}],"draft":null,"quiz":[{"question":"What does an agentic UI assume that a traditional UI does not?","options":["That the user types one question and then waits for one answer","That the software always behaves the same way after each click","That an agent is running, and the human watches and steers it","That the screen is drawn only after all of the work is finished"],"answer":2,"explain":"A traditional UI assumes a human giving commands to software that always behaves the same way. An agentic UI assumes a running agent that the human watches and steers."},{"question":"Why does an agentic UI stream the run instead of returning the final answer at the end?","options":["Each step shown lets the user see progress and catch mistakes","Streaming makes the model generate its whole answer a lot faster","A final answer at the end cannot carry the results of tool calls","A browser cannot receive one large response from the backend"],"answer":0,"explain":"An agent run can take minutes. Streaming each step avoids a blank wait and lets the user stop a run that is going wrong."},{"question":"What problem does AG-UI solve?","options":["It connects an agent to the tools and data it needs to do its work","It lets one agent hand a part of its work to another agent","It makes the model produce fewer tokens for the same answer","It gives all frameworks one shared set of events for the screen"],"answer":3,"explain":"Each framework streams its own event format, which ties the front end to it. AG-UI is one shared contract, so the agent behind the screen can change."},{"question":"In the agent protocol stack, which side of the agent does each protocol connect?","options":["MCP to users, A2A to tools, and AG-UI to other agents","MCP to tools, A2A to other agents, and AG-UI to users","MCP to other agents, A2A to users, and AG-UI to tools","All three of them connect the agent to its tools"],"answer":1,"explain":"MCP connects tools and data, A2A connects other agents, and AG-UI connects the users. A real product often uses all three."},{"question":"In AG-UI, how does a run stop when the agent needs a person's answer?","options":["It ends with a RunError event, and the person must start over","It keeps the run open and sends text events until the reply","It ends with a RunFinished event whose outcome is interrupt","It deletes the thread, and a new thread starts with the reply"],"answer":2,"explain":"The run ends with an interrupt outcome. The next run, on the same thread, carries the person's answer in its resume list."}]}